-- title:
--   Finite faithfully flat descent for the rigidified Pic⁰ presheaf
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $c : C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a morphism of schemes, and let $\varepsilon$ be an element of `SchemeHomOver (𝟙 (Spec (CommRingCat.of R))) c`, that is, a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ whose composite with $c$ is the identity. Assume the hypothesis `hH0`: for every $R$-algebra $A$, the canonical map $A \to \Gamma(C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} A, \mathcal{O})$ — the algebra map for the $A$-algebra structure on global sections induced by the projection $C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ — is bijective. Let $R'$ be an $R$-algebra which is finite as an $R$-module and faithfully flat over $R$, and let $T$ be an object of the category of schemes over $\operatorname{Spec} R$. The conclusion is that the presheaf `relSubPicPresheaf c ε (algEquivZeroCut c ε)` on $(\mathrm{Over}\,\operatorname{Spec} R)^{\mathrm{op}}$ — the subfunctor of the relative Picard presheaf of $(c,\varepsilon)$ whose sections over $t : T_0 \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ are those isomorphism classes of rigidified line bundles $M$ satisfying `FibrewiseAlgEquivZero`, i.e. for every algebraically closed field $k$ and every $s : \operatorname{Spec} k \to T_0$ the pullback of $M.L$ to the fibre at $s$ satisfies `IsAlgEquivZero` — satisfies the sheaf condition `Presieve.IsSheafFor` for the single-morphism presieve generated by the counit of the adjunction `Over.mapPullbackAdj (SmoothProperCurve.specMap R R')` at $T$, namely the projection $T \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} R' \to T$ regarded as a morphism over $\operatorname{Spec} R$. Concretely, every element of the presheaf at $T \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} R'$ that is compatible for this presieve has a unique amalgamation over $T$.
--
--   This is the finite faithfully flat base-change case of the assertion that the rigidified relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ functor of $(c,\varepsilon)$ is a sheaf for the flat topology, with the geometric input $c_*\mathcal{O}_C = \mathcal{O}$ universally isolated as the explicit hypothesis that $A \to \Gamma(C_A,\mathcal{O})$ is bijective for all $R$-algebras $A$. It feeds the construction of a representing object for the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ subfunctor by finite étale descent, and the corresponding sheaf statement for coverings coming from finite étale data.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_RelPicard_isSheafFor_relSubPicPresheaf_algEquivZeroCut_finite_faithfullyFlat_of_bijective_sections.lean

